.TH SESSLINT-REPAIR 1 "" "SessLint 0.5.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-repair \- [writes: output file and manifest, lossy under \-\-policy salvage] Safely repair a session file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint repair [\-o | \-\-output OUTPUT] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-preview] [\-\-policy {conservative,salvage}] [\-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}] [\-\-emit {auto,canonical,vendor}] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-json] [\-\-progress\-json] [\-\-no\-progress] [\-\-plan | \-\-apply\-plan PLAN] [\-\-plan\-out PLAN_OUT] [\-\-from\-scan REPORT.json] [\-\-output\-dir DIR] [\-\-manifest\-dir DIR] [\-\-acknowledge\-side\-effects] [\-\-include\-content] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-seal LEDGER] [\-\-seal\-no\-path] [\-\-seal\-genesis\-of HEX] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose] PATH...
.SH DESCRIPTION
[writes: output file and manifest, lossy under \-\-policy salvage] Safely repair a session file with atomic execution.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Path(s) to source session file(s) or directories. Directories and multiple paths batch\-repair into \-\-output\-dir (mirroring input structure). '\-' reads the source from stdin (max 100 MB; still requires \-\-output unless \-\-dry\-run).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o OUTPUT, \-\-output OUTPUT
Path to output repaired session file
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Plan\-only mode; do not write any files
.TP
.B \-\-preview
Render the structural repair preview (sesslint.preview/v1): content\-free delta rows per plan step, then exit without writing. Incompatible with \-\-output/\-\-plan\-out/\-\-apply\-plan/batch modes.
.TP
.B \-\-policy {conservative,salvage}
Repair policy (choices: conservative, salvage; default: conservative) Choices: conservative, salvage.
.TP
.B \-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}
Session format adapter (default: auto) Choices: auto, canonical, claude\-code\-jsonl, codex\-rollout, openai\-agents.
.TP
.B \-\-emit {auto,canonical,vendor}
Output artifact format. 'auto' (default) emits the input's own format: vendor input produces a drop\-only line\-verbatim write\-back; 'canonical' always emits the canonical session stream. Choices: auto, canonical, vendor. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
Replay validation profile (default: neutral)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output manifest or plan in JSON format
.TP
.B \-\-progress\-json
Emit NDJSON progress events to stderr (stdout stays the result channel)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
Disable interactive progress output on stderr
.TP
.B \-\-plan PLAN, \-\-apply\-plan PLAN
Apply a previously exported plan JSON (sesslint.plan/v1) without re\-planning. The plan is authoritative: \-\-policy/\-\-profile/\-\-adapter overrides are refused, and execution still re\-validates the plan fingerprint and source binding.
.TP
.B \-\-plan\-out PLAN_OUT
Export the computed repair plan (sesslint.plan/v1) to PATH for review or later \-\-apply\-plan. Plan\-only when \-\-output is absent; with \-\-output the exported plan is executed in the same run.
.TP
.B \-\-from\-scan REPORT.json
Batch\-repair files listed in a sesslint scan JSON report; only '~/'\-minimized and absolute paths resolve — '.._<hash>' entries are reported skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-dir DIR
Output root for batch repair modes (mirrors input structure).
.TP
.B \-\-manifest\-dir DIR
Manifest root for batch modes; manifests are named <sha8\-of\-source\-path>.manifest.json. Default: adjacent to each output.
.TP
.B \-\-acknowledge\-side\-effects
Acknowledge tool side\-effects for salvage policy
.TP
.B \-\-include\-content
Embed raw transcript content in manifests (warning: emits raw sensitive data)
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
Explicit config file path (overrides [tool.sesslint] discovery)
.TP
.B \-\-seal LEDGER
Append a tamper\-evident seal line to LEDGER (append\-only hash\-chained verdict record; 'sesslint seal \-\-verify' re\-checks it)
.TP
.B \-\-seal\-no\-path
Omit the artifact path from the seal line (multi\-machine ledgers)
.TP
.B \-\-seal\-genesis\-of HEX
Bind a new ledger's first line to a prior ledger's last entry hash (ledger rotation)
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
a clean session exits 0
(also verification passed / dry-run plan generated)
.TP
.B 1
a session with findings exits 1
(also verification failed / repair refused)
.TP
.B 2
an internal tool error exits 2
(also usage error / invalid flags / I/O failure)
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

